     // typos check\n+                List\u003cString\u003e potentialMatches \u003d StringUtils.findSimilar(tableName, tables.keySet());\n+                if (CollectionUtils.isEmpty(potentialMatches) \u003d\u003d false) {\n+                    message \u003d UnresolvedAttribute.errorMessage(tableName, potentialMatches).replace(\"column\", \"table\");\n+                }\n+                tableNameExpression \u003d new UnresolvedAttribute(tableNameExpression.source(), tableName, null, message);\n+            }\n+            // wrap the table in a local relationship for idiomatic field resolution\n+            else {\n+                localRelation \u003d tableMapAsRelation(source, tables.get(tableName));\n+                // postpone the resolution for ResolveRefs\n+            }\n+\n+            return new Lookup(source, lookup.child(), tableNameExpression, lookup.matchFields(), localRelation);\n+        }\n+\n+        private LocalRelation tableMapAsRelation(Source source, Map\u003cString, Column\u003e mapTable) {","submitted_line":351},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]},{"groundTruth":{"original_line":341,"start_side":"RIGHT","start_line":338,"line":351,"comment_lines":["[][338]","[][339]","[][340]","[][341]","[][342]","[][343]","[][344]","[][345]","[][346]","[][347]","[][348]","[][349]","[][350]","[][351]"],"review_comment":["A trick used in this block, similar to enrich is to pass the user data as a literal and then convert it into a unresolved attribute if it\u0027s not found.","This is consistent with Enrich, but I find it confusing that we allow a general Expression for the table name (resp. for the enrich policy name). At least I\u0027d expect we\u0027d specialize this to a keyword literal if this really needs to be an `Expression`, but this is not an attribute by any means.","Look closer - the block above shows why an Expression is used instead of a Literal."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/analysis/Analyzer.java","id":360